<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<%- include('partials/head', {
  pageTitle: 'Design System - MTG Deck Shuffler',
  additionalFonts: ['Ovo', 'Risque'],
  additionalStyles: [
    '/playmat.css',
    '/game.css',
    '/prepare.css',
    '/deck-selection.css',
    '/design-candidates.css',
    '/design-gallery.css'
  ]
}) %>

<body>
  <div class="design-page">
    <%- include('partials/header', { linksInNewTabs: true }) %>

    <div class="gallery-container">

      <div class="gallery-intro">
        <h1>Design System</h1>
        <p>
          Every specimen below is rendered by the app's own stylesheets — the same
          <code>styles.css</code>, <code>site.css</code>, <code>playmat.css</code>,
          <code>game.css</code>, <code>prepare.css</code> and <code>deck-selection.css</code>
          the real pages load. If a component changes in the app, it changes here. The gallery's
          own chrome (labels, frames, swatch grids) is the only thing styled by
          <code>design-gallery.css</code>, and proposals not yet adopted live in
          <code>design-candidates.css</code>.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">
          Sections are tagged <span class="badge badge-standard">standard</span> where the app is
          already consistent, <span class="badge badge-choose">choose one</span> where more than one
          treatment is in use and you need to pick, and <span class="badge badge-drift">drift</span>
          where there's no standard at all yet.
        </p>
        <nav class="gallery-toc">
          <a href="#color">Color</a>
          <a href="#type">Typography</a>
          <a href="#geometry">Geometry &amp; spacing</a>
          <a href="#buttons">Buttons</a>
          <a href="#focus">Focus states</a>
          <a href="#inputs">Text inputs</a>
          <a href="#surfaces">Surfaces</a>
          <a href="#cards">Cards &amp; playmat</a>
          <a href="#rules">House rules</a>
        </nav>
      </div>

      <!-- ================================================================ -->
      <section class="gallery-section" id="color">
        <h2>Color <span class="badge badge-drift">drift</span></h2>
        <p class="section-note">
          Six named tokens carry the brand, and they're used well where they're used at all — but
          only 46 <code>var()</code> references exist across 2,772 lines of CSS, against
          <strong>57 distinct hex values</strong>. Most of the rest is imported palette: Material
          Design and Bootstrap defaults that arrived one button at a time.
        </p>

